Let $f\in L^1(\R)$ be even and non-negative, with Fourier transform $\hat f$.
Define the radial function $g\colon\R^3\to\R$ by
\begin{align}
g(\bx) := \frac{2}{|\bx|}\int_0^{|\bx|} f(u)\,du,\qquad \bm{x}\neq \bm{0},
\end{align}
with $g(\bm{0})$ defined by continuity.

